  "Name": "Kumar2015-TiO2-SiO2-675",
  "Source": "M. Kumar, N. Kumari, P. K. Rao, V. Karar, S. V. Ramagopal, and A. L. Sharma, \"Multi-layer dielectric thin-film optical filters for beam folding applications,\" Proc. SPIE 9654, 96540F (2015). doi:10.1117/12.2181776 - Sec. 2.1 text below Fig. 1 (p. 2): TiO2 80 nm, SiO2 130 nm; substrate BK7 from Sec. 2.2; indices Table 1",
  "Notes": "Five-layer TiO2/SiO2 folding mirror for red light, peak reflectance at 675 nm at 45 deg (Multilayer II)\nSpecification: Peak reflectance at 675 nm at 45 deg incidence (beam folding, red).\nReported: Text: peak reflectance at 675 nm (45 deg); peak 'close to 80 %'. Fig. 1 simulated (red curve, approximate): R ~15 % at 400 nm, minimum ~10 % near 430 nm, secondary maximum ~22 % near 470 nm, minimum ~9 % near 510 nm, ~45 % at 560 nm, maximum ~77 % around 650-680 nm, ~76 % at 700 nm. Fig. 3 measured (Multilayer II): ~33 % at 415 nm, minimum ~17 % near 445 nm, ~34 % at 495 nm, minimum ~5 % near 555 nm, ~67-68 % at 680-700 nm.\nNotes: Same assumptions as Kumar2015-TiO2-SiO2-480: HLHLH order assumed, TiO2 n = 2.3 (midpoint of 2.2-2.4), unpolarised, 45 deg in air, incoherent BK7 back side included in the paper's simulation. In Fig. 3 'Multilayer II' is the red filter; the paper notes its measured peak dropped slightly, attributed to thickness errors. Total physical thickness 3x80 + 2x130 = 500 nm (not printed).\nLayers from Sec. 2.1 text below Fig. 1 (p. 2): TiO2 80 nm, SiO2 130 nm; substrate BK7 from Sec. 2.2; indices Table 1; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours R peak 79.6 % at 687 nm, 45 deg, with the back surface; paper peak near 675 nm, R ~80 %.",
